# Proton-CachyOS, arm64 build: a Steam compatibility tool for the Adreno 610 (SM6115), for its
# DXVK-Sarek.
#
# Read by /usr/lib/retroforge/steam-compat-tools, which runs when the player presses Download or Update
# in Apps > Steam Client > "CachyOS Proton arm64" (retroforge-steam-cachyos), and when a store game needs
# a Proton. It downloads the release into the player's home and installs it as
# <Steam root>/compatibilitytools.d/<dir>/, with DXVK-Sarek on in it where the GPU needs it (the
# SM4450's Adreno 613; the SM6115 takes proton-armv8.pin).
# Steam lists it from its next start on. Nothing selects it: the player does, per game or as the Steam
# Play default (docs/steam-arm64.md).
#
# Why: every upstream DXVK (1.10.3, 2.x, 3.x) needs multiViewport, which Turnip does not give the A610.
# Today it only gets it because session.conf sets TU_DEBUG=noconform there, which Mesa 26.3 removes
# (and Mesa 82b86896 keeps multiViewport off on a6xx_gen1_low). Proton-CachyOS carries DXVK-Sarek, which
# works without it, and its arm64 build has Sarek as ARM64EC. PROTON_DXVK_SAREK=1 turns it on. Its
# maintainers call the arm64 build untested.
#
# Not in the image: the tarball is ~356 MB and unpacks to ~2.2 GB, and a root slot is 2 GB.
# Its toolmanifest.vdf requires tool appid 4185400 (Steam Linux Runtime 4.0, arm64), which Steam
# downloads itself. A local scan of cachyos-11.0-20261005-slr found nothing beyond ARMv8.0 except LSE
# atomics (kernel/patches/0025 covers those), apart from libraries that pick their code path at run
# time. A later release is not scanned before players get it.
#
# A CHANNEL, NOT A VERSION. This names where releases come from and which build, and the device
# resolves what is published now: at each `steam` start while the setting is on, ONE request to
# GitHub's API (60 an hour are allowed without a token), and the newest release that has the asset
# below and its .sha512sum. Newest = the highest Proton version, then the latest published:
# cachyos-10.0-sunset-slr came out a week after cachyos-11.0-20260601-slr and is not an update. Drafts
# and prereleases are skipped. The tarball is checked against that .sha512sum and the sha256 GitHub
# lists for it. Offline, rate limited or on any API error, the installed release stays. A new release
# replaces the old one in place (in the same run, or at the next start while a game runs from the old
# one), under the same name, so a game set to the tool keeps it.
#
# Fields (one per line, `key: value`, no trailing comments):
#   name          the family, written into each folder's .retroforge-pin. A folder without that marker
#                 is never touched.
#   releases      GitHub's API for the repo's releases: ?per_page=20 is added for the channel,
#                 /tags/<tag> for a tag.
#   asset         the tarball, as a glob. Its .sha512sum is <name without .tar.xz>.sha512sum next to
#                 it, and its top folder is <name without .tar.xz>.
#   dir           the folder under compatibilitytools.d AND the tool's internal name: its
#                 compatibilitytool.vdf is rewritten so. Steam keys a game's tool (CompatToolMapping in
#                 config.vdf) by that name, so a game set to it keeps it across releases. Changing it
#                 makes every player select the tool again.
#   display_name  what Steam shows for it.
#   tag           OPTIONAL: hold one release instead of following the channel, for a reproducible
#                 build or to keep players off a bad release (e.g. tag: cachyos-11.0-20261005-slr).
#                 Once that release is installed, nothing is asked.
#   sha512        OPTIONAL, only with tag: the tarball's sha512, used instead of its .sha512sum.
#
# Resolved on 2026-10-16: cachyos-11.0-20261005-slr, proton-cachyos-11.0-20261005-slr-arm64.tar.xz,
# 356312716 bytes, sha512 81ca1b66...b1c0fa (its .sha512sum), sha256 e59b646e...cd06c37 (GitHub's).
name: proton-cachyos-arm64
releases: https://api.github.com/repos/CachyOS/proton-cachyos/releases
asset: proton-cachyos-*-slr-arm64.tar.xz
dir: proton-cachyos-arm64-retroforge
display_name: Proton-CachyOS arm64 (RetroForge)
